<p>
  The thread is a <code>Y.Array</code> named <code>messages</code>. Each
  message is a <code>Y.Map</code> with its text, author, and time, plus a
  nested <code>Y.Map</code> of reactions keyed by person. Two people reacting
  to the same message write different keys, so both reactions are kept.
  Choosing your reaction again deletes your key. The room keeps the last 200
  messages.
</p>
<p>
  What you type before you send isn't in the document. It's in your awareness
  state, which the server passes to the room but doesn't save, so the other
  window sees each character as you type it and a closed tab leaves nothing
  behind. Enter sends, and Shift+Enter starts a new line. Click or long-press a
  message to react.
</p>
